ww.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nArchive all prior ingredient nodes, including false LB expansion, combined yeast amounts and copied or chemically inexact annotations, in append-only history. New nodes follow this exact source's stage and label; other unchanged chemical annotations are preserved, not recertified.\\n\\nSource-scoped recipe inputs supersede unsupported flattened concentrations and false LB identities. All prior history and permanent IDs remain unchanged; unquantified quantities remain unknown. No taxa-media association is added.\", \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\", \"snippet\": \"DL-2-Methylbutyric acid\"}, {\"old_field\": \"variant_children\", \"field\": \"variant_children\", \"old\": null, \"new\": [{\"id\": \"CultureMech:003939\", \"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/archaea/KOMODO_119_METHANOBACTERIUM_medium.yaml\", \"name\": \"methanobacterium_medium\", \"relationship\": \"DERIVED_FROM\", \"notes\": \"KOMODO explicitly links DSMZ 119, but its source-specific rates, nulls and metadata are not an exact copy of the original. DERIVED_FROM denotes documented source derivation, not a measured growth association.\", \"evidence\": [{\"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=119\", \"supports\": \"SUPPORT\", \"snippet\": \"Instructions: http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\", \"explanation\": \"variant_children: KOMODO explicitly links DSMZ 119, but its source-specific rates, nulls and metadata are not an exact copy of the original. DERIVED_FROM denotes documented source derivation, not a measured growth association. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=original recipe table/text; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:57.185386+00:00; capture SHA256=18f364d4c03a22fb2752d836ec167b87f9755fa4a1cf25023c5993c00d8e6bb6.\"}]}], \"status\": \"add\", \"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=119\", \"snippet\": \"Instructions: http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\"}, {\"old_field\": \"parent_media\", \"field\": \"parent_media\", \"old\": {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/gudongella_medium.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"CONCENTRATION_VARIANT\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:000646\", \"name\": \"gudongella_medium\", \"notes\": \"Reviewed Methanobacterium medium as a concentration variant of Gudongella medium with bicarbonate as the curated axis.\"}, \"new\": {\"id\": \"CultureMech:000646\", \"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/gudongella_medium.yaml\", \"name\": \"gudongella_medium\", \"relationship\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"notes\": \"Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn.\", \"evidence\": [{\"reference\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/119c\", \"supports\": \"SUPPORT\", \"snippet\": \"\\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.8 and dispense medium under 100% N2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\", \"explanation\": \"parent_media: Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[0].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:29:20.378790+00:00; capture SHA256=e6fb6c737e1297709b90d4a1d7fbdc90870ce6cf52d8f47c291de24e952e970b.\\n\\nAdditional exact excerpt: \\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.8 and dispense medium under 100% N2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\\nvariant_relationship: Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[0].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:29:20.378790+00:00; capture SHA256=e6fb6c737e1297709b90d4a1d7fbdc90870ce6cf52d8f47c291de24e952e970b.\\n\\nAdditional exact excerpt: \\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.8 and dispense medium under 100% N2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\\nvariant_modifications: Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[0].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:29:20.378790+00:00; capture SHA256=e6fb6c737e1297709b90d4a1d7fbdc90870ce6cf52d8f47c291de24e952e970b.\"}]}, \"status\": \"correct\", \"reference\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/119c\", \"snippet\": \"\\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.8 and dispense medium under 100% N2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": \"variant_relationship\", \"field\": \"variant_relationship\", \"old\": \"CONCENTRATION_VARIANT\", \"new\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"status\": \"correct\", \"reference\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/119c\", \"snippet\": \"\\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.8 and dispense medium under 100% N2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": \"variant_modifications\", \"field\": \"variant_modifications\", \"old\": [\"Reviewed Gudongella/Methanobacterium pair; child keeps the same complex anaerobic base, sludge, volatile acids, tryptone, trace elements, and supplements effectively unchanged but increases NaHCO3 from 0.5 to 3.98804 g/L.\"], \"new\": [\"Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn.\"], \"status\": \"correct\", \"reference\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/119c\", \"snippet\": \"\\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.8 and dispense medium under 100% N2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": \"notes\", \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": \"Source: DSMZ | Link: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\\n\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\", \"new\": \"Source: DSMZ | Link: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommer