ddition: 10 ml = 0.01 L of this prepared stock. This is an addition volume, not stock strength or final-medium concentration. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].recipe[14]; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: {\n                        \"recipe_order\": 16,\n                        \"compound\": \"Methanol\",\n                        \"compound_id\": 226,\n                        \"attribute\": \"15% v/v\",\n                        \"amount\": 10,\n                        \"unit\": \"ml\",\n                        \"g_l\": 7.88845,\n                        \"mmol_l\": 246.191,\n                        \"optional\": 0\n                    }\nsolutions[6].preferred_term: Receiving-medium addition: 10 ml = 0.01 L of this prepared stock. This is an addition volume, not stock strength or final-medium concentration. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].recipe[14]; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: {\n                        \"recipe_order\": 16,\n                        \"compound\": \"Methanol\",\n                        \"compound_id\": 226,\n                        \"attribute\": \"15% v/v\",\n                        \"amount\": 10,\n                        \"unit\": \"ml\",\n                        \"g_l\": 7.88845,\n                        \"mmol_l\": 246.191,\n                        \"optional\": 0\n                    }\nsolutions[6].name: Receiving-medium addition: 10 ml = 0.01 L of this prepared stock. This is an addition volume, not stock strength or final-medium concentration. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].recipe[14]; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: \"Dissolve ingredients except methanol, bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Adjust pH of medium to 7.2 and sparge with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Then dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes to 30% v/v of their volume and autoclave. Add methanol (from 15% v/v stock solution), cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas and bicarbonate from a sterile anoxic stock solution prepared under 80% N2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 7.6, if necessary.\"\npreparation_steps: Only the main-stage instructions remain at recipe root; stock preparation instructions are preserved on their named solution descriptors. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[0].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: \"After inoculation, add sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture to 0.5 bar overpressure. After growth becomes visible overpressure of 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture can be increased to 1 bar.\"\npreparation_steps: Only the main-stage instructions remain at recipe root; stock preparation instructions are preserved on their named solution descriptors. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[1].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: \"Note: Use 10% (v/v) as inoculum.\"\npreparation_steps: Only the main-stage instructions remain at recipe root; stock preparation instructions are preserved on their named solution descriptors. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[2].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: {\n                        \"recipe_order\": 16,\n                        \"compound\": \"Methanol\",\n                        \"compound_id\": 226,\n                        \"attribute\": \"15% v/v\",\n                        \"amount\": 10,\n                        \"unit\": \"ml\",\n                        \"g_l\": 7.88845,\n                        \"mmol_l\": 246.191,\n                        \"optional\": 0\n                    }\nparent_media: Withdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].recipe[14]; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: {\n                        \"recipe_order\": 16,\n                        \"compound\": \"Methanol\",\n                        \"compound_id\": 226,\n                        \"attribute\": \"15% v/v\",\n                        \"amount\": 10,\n                        \"unit\": \"ml\",\n                        \"g_l\": 7.88845,\n                        \"mmol_l\": 246.191,\n                        \"optional\": 0\n                    }\nvariant_relationship: Withdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].recipe[14]; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa.\n\nAdditional exact excerpt: {\n                        \"recipe_order\": 16,\n                        \"compound\": \"Methanol\",\n                        \"compound_id\": 226,\n                        \"attribute\": \"15% v/v\",\n                        \"amount\": 10,\n                        \"unit\": \"ml\",\n                        \"g_l\": 7.88845,\n                        \"mmol_l\": 246.191,\n                        \"optional\": 0\n                    }\nvariant_modifications: Withdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].recipe[14]; accessed=2026-10-09T02:28:58.050679+00:00; capture SHA256=5ad26da1456972fe0566ef0ea37cb4d94df291c828b5a7bc809dea7e445408fa."
