uperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nArchive all prior ingredient nodes, including false LB expansion, combined yeast amounts and copied or chemically inexact annotations, in append-only history. New nodes follow this exact source's stage and label; other unchanged chemical annotations are preserved, not recertified.\\n\\nSource-scoped recipe inputs supersede unsupported flattened concentrations and false LB identities. All prior history and permanent IDs remain unchanged; unquantified quantities remain unknown. No taxa-media association is added.\", \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119c.pdf\", \"snippet\": \"DL-2-Methylbutyric acid\"}, {\"old_field\": \"ingredients[25].concentration\", \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": {\"value\": \"10.0\", \"unit\": \"G_PER_L\"}, \"new\": \"Source: DSMZ | Link: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119c.pdf\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nArchive all prior ingredient nodes, including false LB expansion, combined yeast amounts and copied or chemically inexact annotations, in append-only history. New nodes follow this exact source's stage and label; other unchanged chemical annotations are preserved, not recertified.\\n\\nSource-scoped recipe inputs supersede unsupported flattened concentrations and false LB identities. All prior history and permanent IDs remain unchanged; unquantified quantities remain unknown. No taxa-media association is added.\", \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119c.pdf\", \"snippet\": \"DL-2-Methylbutyric acid\"}, {\"old_field\": \"variant_children\", \"field\": \"variant_children\", \"old\": [{\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/methanobacterium_medium.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"CONCENTRATION_VARIANT\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:000643\", \"name\": \"methanobacterium_medium\", \"notes\": \"Reviewed Gudongella/Methanobacterium pair; child keeps the same complex anaerobic base, sludge, volatile acids, tryptone, trace elements, and supplements effectively unchanged but increases NaHCO3 from 0.5 to 3.98804 g/L.\"}], \"new\": [{\"id\": \"CultureMech:000643\", \"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/archaea/methanobacterium_medium.yaml\", \"name\": \"methanobacterium_medium\", \"relationship\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"notes\": \"Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn.\", \"evidence\": [{\"reference\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/119\", \"supports\": \"SUPPORT\", \"snippet\": \"\\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.5 and dispense medium under 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials to 30% of their volume and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\", \"explanation\": \"variant_children: Retain this existing family candidate as UNCERTAIN, not a proven direction of derivation or a bicarbonate-only variant. DSMZ 119 uses 4 g bicarbonate and H2/CO2 preparation; DSMZ 119c uses 0.5 g and N2 preparation. Both preserve distinct stock scopes; the old LB/tryptone assertion is withdrawn. No unstated density, final volume, percent basis or chemical identifier is inferred. Locator=data.solutions[0].steps[0].step; accessed=2026-10-09T02:29:12.183202+00:00; capture SHA256=2ef0379b2f6f083499de9281386d962be27ba59fcba5135710f46288227d666e.\"}]}], \"status\": \"correct\", \"reference\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/119\", \"snippet\": \"\\\"Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, cysteine and sulfide. Sparge medium with 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Add and dissolve bicarbonate, adjust pH to 6.5 and dispense medium under 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials to 30% of their volume and autoclave. Add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to use check pH of complete medium and adjust to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary.\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": \"notes\", \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": \"Source: DSMZ | Link: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119c.pdf\\n\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\", \"new\": \"Source: DSMZ | Link: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119c.pdf\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nArchive all prior ingredient nodes, including false LB expansion, combined yeast amounts and copied or chemically inexact annotations, in append-only history. New nodes follow this exact source's stage and label; other unchanged chemical annotations are preserved, not recertified.\\n\\nSource-scoped recipe inputs supersede unsupported flattened concentrations and false LB identities. All prior history and permanent IDs remain unchanged; unquantified quantities remain unknown. No taxa-media association is added.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119c.pdf\", \"snippet\": \"DL-2-Methylbutyric acid\"}]"
