\"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_15163\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/medium_119_modified_for_dsm_3468.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:003919\", \"name\": \"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_3468\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/medium_119_modified_for_dsm_4855.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:003920\", \"name\": \"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_4855\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/medium_119_modified_for_dsm_6216.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:003921\", \"name\": \"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_6216\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/medium_119_modified_for_dsm_7057.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:003922\", \"name\": \"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_7057\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/medium_119_modified_for_dsm_7256.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:003923\", \"name\": \"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_7256\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/medium_119_modified_for_dsm_9575.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:003924\", \"name\": \"medium_119_modified_for_dsm_9575\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/methanomassiliicoccus_medium.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:000645\", \"name\": \"methanomassiliicoccus_medium\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}], \"new\": \"pH buffer: NaOH | Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 119 | DSMZ Medium: 119 (mediadive.medium:119) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nProvider aerobic=true and pH=7.5 metadata disagree with the linked DSMZ anoxic preparation and complete-medium pH 6.8-7.0. Retain provider scope without asserting a resolved oxygen requirement.\\n\\nThe linked original uses anoxic preparation; its individual stock inputs and strain instructions must not silently replace this provider's reported medium rates.\\n\\nArchive all prior ingredient nodes, including false LB expansion, combined yeast amounts and copied or chemically inexact annotations, in append-only history. New nodes follow this exact source's stage and label; other unchanged chemical annotations are preserved, not recertified.\\n\\nWithdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity.\\n\\nWithdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity.\\n\\nSource-scoped recipe inputs supersede unsupported flattened concentrations and false LB identities. All prior history and permanent IDs remain unchanged; unquantified quantities remain unknown. No taxa-media association is added.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=119\", \"snippet\": \"Instructions: http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"pH buffer: NaOH | Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 119 | DSMZ Medium: 119 (mediadive.medium:119) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nProvider aerobic=true and pH=7.5 metadata disagree with the linked DSMZ anoxic preparation and complete-medium pH 6.8-7.0. Retain provider scope without asserting a resolved oxygen requirement.\\n\\nThe linked original uses anoxic preparation; its individual stock inputs and strain instructions must not silently replace this provider's reported medium rates.\\n\\nArchive all prior ingredient nodes, including false LB expansion, combined yeast amounts and copied or chemically inexact annotations, in append-only history. New nodes follow this exact source's stage and label; other unchanged chemical annotations are preserved, not recertified.\\n\\nWithdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity.\\n\\nWithdraw the unsupported K119/DSMZ119b exact-duplicate edge: K119 links original DSMZ119, whereas DSMZ119b includes methanol and selenite-tungstate and different bicarbonate, water and preparation. Their old copied ingredient signatures are not source evidence of identity.\\n\\nSource-scoped recipe inputs supersede unsupported flattened concentrations and false LB identities. All prior history and permanent IDs remain unchanged; unquantified quantities remain unknown. No taxa-media association is added.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119b.pdf\", \"snippet\": \"Methanol (15% v/v)\"}, {\"old_field\": \"notes\", \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": \"pH buffer: NaOH | Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 119 | DSMZ Medium: 119 (mediadive.medium:119) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\", \"new\": \"pH buffer: NaOH | Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 119 | DSMZ Medium: 119 (mediadive.medium:119) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nProvider aerobic=true and pH=7.5 metadata disagree with the linked DSMZ anoxic preparation and complete-medium pH 6.8-7.0. Retain provider scope without asserting a resolved oxygen requir