erverSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=161\", \"snippet\": \"Yeast extract (Difco) Yeast extract rich-peptone# 1.00 null\"}, {\"old_field\": \"ingredients[7].notes\", \"field\": \"ingredients[42].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Exact displayed Gram Amounts and nulls; not rounded molar columns or combined SEED rows. Even clarified-rumen-fluid grams are this provider's assertion, not a density conversion from original ml inputs Exact heading: Gram & Mol amounts are per Liter of medium.\", \"status\": \"correct\", \"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=161\", \"snippet\": \"Yeast extract (Difco) Yeast extract rich-peptone# 1.00 null\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 161 | DSMZ Medium: 161 (mediadive.medium:161) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance, not a current formulation claim:\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nPreserve this provider's exact displayed Gram Amounts and nulls. The 300.00 g/L clarified-rumen-fluid row is a provider assertion, not a conversion from original ml. No density, stereochemistry, missing amount or growth association is inferred.\\n\\nRetain this provider's pH6.5. Its aerobic flag is source metadata, not a verified cultivation condition; the linked original describes anoxic preparation.\\n\\nThe linked original uses anoxic preparation and H2/CO2 incubation. This conflicts with KOMODO's aerobic flag; preserve the source distinction rather than certify either as biological growth evidence.\\n\\nComplete inspected source rows define this reconstruction. Archive false LB expansions, flattened quantities and placeholders in append-only history. Preserve earlier supported evidence exactly; unrelated chemical annotations are not recertified.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=161\", \"snippet\": \"Gram & Mol amounts are per Liter of medium.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 161 | DSMZ Medium: 161 (mediadive.medium:161) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance, not a current formulation claim:\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nPreserve this provider's exact displayed Gram Amounts and nulls. The 300.00 g/L clarified-rumen-fluid row is a provider assertion, not a conversion from original ml. No density, stereochemistry, missing amount or growth association is inferred.\\n\\nRetain this provider's pH6.5. Its aerobic flag is source metadata, not a verified cultivation condition; the linked original describes anoxic preparation.\\n\\nThe linked original uses anoxic preparation and H2/CO2 incubation. This conflicts with KOMODO's aerobic flag; preserve the source distinction rather than certify either as biological growth evidence.\\n\\nComplete inspected source rows define this reconstruction. Archive false LB expansions, flattened quantities and placeholders in append-only history. Preserve earlier supported evidence exactly; unrelated chemical annotations are not recertified.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=161\", \"snippet\": \"Is Aerobic: true\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Source: KOMODO ModelSEED | ID: 161 | DSMZ Medium: 161 (mediadive.medium:161) | Aerobic: Yes\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance, not a current formulation claim:\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nPreserve this provider's exact displayed Gram Amounts and nulls. The 300.00 g/L clarified-rumen-fluid row is a provider assertion, not a conversion from original ml. No density, stereochemistry, missing amount or growth association is inferred.\\n\\nRetain this provider's pH6.5. Its aerobic flag is source metadata, not a verified cultivation condition; the linked original describes anoxic preparation.\\n\\nThe linked original uses anoxic preparation and H2/CO2 incubation. This conflicts with KOMODO's aerobic flag; preserve the source distinction rather than certify either as biological growth evidence.\\n\\nComplete inspected source rows define this reconstruction. Archive false LB expansions, flattened quantities and placeholders in append-only history. Preserve earlier supported evidence exactly; unrelated chemical annotations are not recertified.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium161.pdf\", \"snippet\": \"Dissolve ingredients (except bicarbonate, vitamins, cysteine and sulfide) and sparge\\nmedium for 30 - 45 min with 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture to make it anoxic. Add and\\ndissolve bicarbonate and adjust pH to 6.8, then distribute under same gas atmosphere into\\nanoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. After sterilization add cysteine\\nand sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions autoclaved under 100% N2 gas atmosphere.\\nVitamins are prepared under 100% N2 gas atmosphere and sterilized by filtration. Adjust\\npH of complete medium to 6.5. For incubation use sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas\\nmixture at two atmospheres of pressure.\"}, {\"old_field\": \"variant_children\", \"field\": \"variant_children\", \"old\": [{\"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/methanofollis_medium.yaml\", \"relationship\": \"SOURCE_DUPLICATE\", \"id\": \"CultureMech:001100\", \"name\": \"methanofollis_medium\", \"notes\": \"Same ingredient and concentration signature; review as possible duplicate source record.\"}], \"new\": null, \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=161\", \"snippet\": \"Instructions: http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium161.pdf\"}, {\"old_field\": \"parent_media\", \"field\": \"parent_media\", \"old\": null, \"new\": {\"id\": \"CultureMech:001100\", \"path\": \"data/normalized_yaml/archaea/methanofollis_medium.yaml\", \"name\": \"methanofollis_medium\", \"relationship\": \"DERIVED_FROM\", \"notes\": \"KOMODO explicitly derives from DSMZ161 but preserves a distinct source title, displayed rates, nulls, chemical forms and stock scopes. DERIVED_FROM is source provenance, not exact formulation identity, biological equivalence or a new growth claim. Correct stale bacterial paths to the current exact archaea paths.\", \"evidence\": [{\"reference\": \"https://komodo.modelseed.org/komodo/servlet/KomodoTomcatServerSideUtilitiesModelSeed?MediaInfo=161\", \"supports\": \"SUPPORT\", \"snippet\": \"Instructions: http://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium161.pdf\", \"explanation\": \"parent_media: KOMODO explicitly derives from DSMZ161 but preserves a distinct source title, displayed rates, nulls, chemical forms and stock scopes. DERIVED_FROM is source provenance, not exact formulation identity, biological equivalence 