reparation volume is not independently established; the unsupported g/L assertion is withdrawn, not replaced by an assumed one-liter concentration.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Isovaleric acid 0.5 g\"}, {\"old_field\": \"ingredients[22].concentration\", \"field\": \"solutions[3].composition[3].concentration\", \"old\": {\"value\": \"0.5\", \"unit\": \"G_PER_L\"}, \"new\": null, \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M258\", \"snippet\": \"{\\n          \\\"component_name\\\": \\\"Isobutyric acid\\\",\\n          \\\"volume\\\": 0.5,\\n          \\\"unit\\\": \\\"g\\\",\\n          \\\"gmo\\\": \\\"http://purl.jp/bio/10/gmo/GMO_001184\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[3].composition[3].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Role: Carbon source; Properties: Organic compound, Defined component, Simple component\\n\\nSource batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the unsupported g/L assertion is withdrawn, not replaced by an assumed one-liter concentration.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Isobutyric acid 0.5 g\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[3].composition[4].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Source batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the source batch amount is retained without asserting a final concentration.\", \"status\": \"add\", \"reference\": \"https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M258\", \"snippet\": \"{\\n          \\\"component_name\\\": \\\"\\u03b1-Methylbutyric acid\\\",\\n          \\\"volume\\\": 0.5,\\n          \\\"unit\\\": \\\"g\\\",\\n          \\\"gmo\\\": \\\"http://purl.jp/bio/10/gmo/GMO_001495\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[3].composition[4].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Source batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the source batch amount is retained without asserting a final concentration.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"\\u03b1-Methylbutyric acid 0.5 g\"}, {\"old_field\": \"ingredients[26].concentration\", \"field\": \"solutions[3].solutions[0].concentration\", \"old\": {\"value\": \"variable\", \"unit\": \"VARIABLE\"}, \"new\": null, \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M258\", \"snippet\": \"{\\n          \\\"component_name\\\": \\\"NaOH\\\",\\n          \\\"gmo\\\": \\\"http://purl.jp/bio/10/gmo/GMO_001300\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[3].solutions[0].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Properties: Defined component, Inorganic compound, Solution\\n\\nConcentrated NaOH adjusts only the fatty-acid stock to pH 7.5; no fixed dose or numeric strength is given. Removed the unsupported VARIABLE placeholder.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Adjust pH to 7.5 with concentrated NaOH solution.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[3].preparation_notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Adjust pH to 7.5 with concentrated NaOH solution.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Adjust pH to 7.5 with concentrated NaOH solution.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[4].preparation_notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\"}, {\"old_field\": \"ingredients[7].concentration\", \"field\": \"solutions[4].composition[0].concentration\", \"old\": {\"value\": \"0.5\", \"unit\": \"G_PER_L\"}, \"new\": null, \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M258\", \"snippet\": \"{\\n          \\\"component_name\\\": \\\"Na2S\\u30fb9H2O\\\",\\n          \\\"volume\\\": 0.5,\\n          \\\"unit\\\": \\\"g\\\",\\n          \\\"gmo\\\": \\\"http://purl.jp/bio/10/gmo/GMO_001014\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[4].composition[0].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Role: Reducing agent; Properties: Inorganic compound, Defined component, Simple component\\n\\nSource batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the unsupported g/L assertion is withdrawn, not replaced by an assumed one-liter concentration. This is the contribution specified for the receiving medium batch, not the mass for preparing an unspecified volume of stock.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Na2S\\u00b79H2O 0.5 g\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[4].composition[0].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Role: Reducing agent; Properties: Inorganic compound, Defined component, Simple component\\n\\nSource batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the unsupported g/L assertion is withdrawn, not replaced by an assumed one-liter concentration. This is the contribution specified for the receiving medium batch, not the mass for preparing an unspecified volume of stock.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[5].preparation_notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\"}, {\"old_field\": \"ingredients[13].concentration\", \"field\": \"solutions[5].composition[0].concentration\", \"old\": {\"value\": \"0.5\", \"unit\": \"G_PER_L\"}, \"new\": null, \"status\": \"remove_unsupported\", \"reference\": \"https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M258\", \"snippet\": \"{\\n          \\\"component_name\\\": \\\"L--Cysteine\\u30fbHCl\\u30fbH2O\\\",\\n          \\\"volume\\\": 0.5,\\n          \\\"unit\\\": \\\"g\\\",\\n          \\\"gmo\\\": \\\"http://purl.jp/bio/10/gmo/GMO_001205\\\"\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[5].composition[0].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Properties: Defined component, Simple component, Organic compound\\n\\nSource batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the unsupported g/L assertion is withdrawn, not replaced by an assumed one-liter concentration. This is the contribution specified for the receiving medium batch, not the mass for preparing an unspecified volume of stock.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"L-Cysteine\\u00b7HCl\\u00b7H2O 0.5 g\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"solutions[5].composition[0].notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Properties: Defined component, Simple component, Organic compound\\n\\nSource batch input: 0.5 g. Final preparation volume is not independently established; the unsupported g/L assertion is withdrawn, not replaced by an assumed one-liter concentration. This is the contribution specified for the receiving medium batch, not the mass for preparing an unspecified volume of stock.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"preparation_steps[0].description\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Mix ingredients, except NaHCO3, L-cysteine\\u00b7HCl\\u00b7H2O and Na2S\\u00b79H2O, and adjust pH to 6.5.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Mix ingredients, except NaHCO3, L-cysteine\\u00b7HCl\\u00b7H2O and Na2S\\u00b79H2O, and adjust pH to 6.5.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"preparation_steps[1].description\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Bring to a boil for 5-10 sec, then, cool down under a stream of H2-CO2 (80:20, v/v) and add NaHCO3 to the medium.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Bring to a boil for 5-10 sec, then, cool down under a stream of H2-CO2 (80:20, v/v) and add NaHCO3 to the medium.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"preparation_steps[2].description\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Dispense the medium into suitable culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml of the medium in 120 ml serum bottles) under a stream of H2-CO2 (80:20, v/v) and seal with butyl rubber stoppers.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Dispense the medium into suitable culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml of the medium in 120 ml serum bottles) under a stream of H2-CO2 (80:20, v/v) and seal with butyl rubber stoppers.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"preparation_steps[3].description\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"After autoclaving, stand the medium overnight.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"After autoclaving, stand the medium overnight.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"preparation_steps[4].description\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Separately autoclave cysteine\\u00b7HCl and Na2S\\u00b79H2O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N2 atmosphere.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"preparation_steps[5].description\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add the L-cysteine\\u00b7HCl\\u00b7H2O and Na2S\\u00b79H2O solutions.\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add the L-cysteine\\u00b7HCl\\u00b7H2O and Na2S\\u00b79H2O solutions.\"}, {\"old_field\": null, \"field\": \"notes\", \"old\": null, \"new\": \"Source: https://togomedium.org/medium/M258\\nOriginal source: JCM - JCM_M266\\nOriginal URL: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\\n\\nSuperseded historical provenance (not a current formulation claim):\\nCommercial Product: LB Medium (Luria-Bertani, Miller formulation)\\nSupplier: Multiple suppliers (Difco, Sigma, etc.)\\nCatalog: Multiple (L3522 Sigma, 244520 BD)\\nSource: https://www.laboratorynotes.com/preparation-of-luria-bertani-lb-miller-broth/\\nAccessed: 2026-03-28\\n\\nConstituent composition researched from product specification.\\n\\nThe earlier LB commercial-product expansion was incorrect for M258/JCM266: three unrelated LB constituents are removed and alpha-methylbutyric acid is restored in the fatty-acid stock at the source batch amount, 0.5 g. The historical supplier paragraph above is retained only as superseded provenance. No chemical grounding is assigned to the restored ingredient.\\n\\nOriginal post-inoculation instruction: Pressurize the inoculated bottles to 200 kPa H2-CO2 (80:20, v/v).\", \"status\": \"evidence_only\", \"reference\": \"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266\", \"snippet\": \"Pressurize the inoculated bottles to 200 kPa H2-CO2 (80:20, v/v).\"}]"
        }
      ],
